cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "RAPI: Regime-Aware Process Intelligence"
message: "If you use this workflow, software, or associated materials in research or derivative work, please cite it using the metadata below."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Winiski"
    given-names: "Jake"

abstract: >
  RAPI (Regime-Aware Process Intelligence) is an open workflow for
  learning in nonstationary process systems. The workflow combines
  rolling local models, global modeling perspectives, dimensionality
  reduction, anomaly detection, and interpretability methods to help
  identify evolving relationships and persistent structure in changing
  systems. Included datasets are synthetic and intended solely for
  demonstration of methodology.

keywords:
  - process intelligence
  - regime-aware learning
  - nonstationary systems
  - statistical learning
  - machine learning
  - manufacturing analytics
  - process development
  - adaptive learning
  - experimental design
  - anomaly detection

